# Git Workflow

## Branch Naming

- `feature/{id}-{short-desc}` — new functionality
- `fix/{id}-{short-desc}` — bug fixes
- `chore/{short-desc}` — maintenance, tooling, config

Examples: `feature/KG-42-spec-editor`, `fix/KG-88-auth-cookie-expiry`, `chore/upgrade-bun`.

## Commit Format

```
type(scope): description
```

Types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `test`, `docs`, `chore`, `style`, `perf`.

Scope matches the workspace or module: `client`, `server`, `shared`, `auth`, `graph`, `db`.

Examples:
- `feat(graph): add bidirectional edge creation`
- `fix(auth): refresh token on 401 before retry`
- `test(server): add integration tests for spec CRUD`

## PR Conventions

- Small, focused PRs — one feature or fix per PR.
- Always include tests for changed behavior.
- PR title follows commit format. Body explains *why*, not *what*.
- Link related issues in the PR description.
